)^{x-1}p, & x=1,2,3,… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, $X∼\\text{Geom}(0.7),$ so the distribution of $X$ in this case is\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}{(0.3)}^{x-1}(0.7), & x=1,2,3… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThere are infinitely many values of $X$ such that $X>3.$ However, we can simplify the computation by using the complement instead:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>3) & =1-P(X\\le 3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the complement, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 3) & =P(X\\in {1,2,3}) \\\\  & =P(X=1)+P(X=2)+P(X=3) \\\\  & =f(1)+f(2)+f(3) \\\\  & ={(0.3)}^{0}(0.7)+{(0.3)}^{1}(0.7)+{(0.3)}^{2}(0.7) \\\\  & =0.973.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>3) & =1-P(X\\le 3) \\\\  & =1-0.973 \\\\  & =0.027.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535726 true] [17592186363426 1000 #edb/ref 17592186363427 13194139535726 true] [17592186363426 1000 #edb/ref 17592186363428 13194139535726 true] [17592186363426 1000 #edb/ref 17592186363429 13194139535726 true] [17592186363426 1000 #edb/ref 17592186363430 13194139535726 true] [17592186363426 1000 #edb/ref 17592186363431 13194139535726 true] [17592186363426 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535726 true] [17592186363426 1041 "selection" 13194139535726 true] [17592186363426 1104 #edb/ref 17592186363428 13194139535726 true] [17592186363426 1110 #uuid "a754b1a4-788e-5709-8a0e-9d1d9dba3b84" 13194139535726 true] [17592186363427 1034 "0.973" 13194139535726 true] [17592186363427 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535726 true] [17592186363427 1111 #uuid "d49af3ed-e963-5844-8f75-83a434537a1d" 13194139535726 true] [17592186363428 1034 "0.027" 13194139535726 true] [17592186363428 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535726 true] [17592186363428 1111 #uuid "1841346a-4636-586d-9b64-9994661d90e9" 13194139535726 true] [17592186363429 1034 "0.908" 13194139535726 true] [17592186363429 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535726 true] [17592186363429 1111 #uuid "c494f012-1182-5589-8e43-bd03